{%- comment -%}
  ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  OTODOR Snippet: Model Price Seed  (published offer pricing, per model)
  Sibling of otodor-spec-model-seed — same idea, applied to money.
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Purpose:   Supply a model's PUBLISHED offer pricing wherever the product's
             own price metafields are not populated yet, so the offer panel
             reads the same figures on every surface.

  IT IS THE WEAKEST SOURCE. Consumers resolve in this order:

      product metafield  →  MODEL SEED  →  Shopify product price  →  nothing

  Populating `custom.effective_price` / `custom.deal_price` in admin (or
  giving the product a real Shopify price) silently overrides it, one product
  at a time; this file is deleted when the last model is covered.

  IT IS NOT A CHECKOUT PRICE. These are the advertised campaign figures the
  client published. What a customer actually pays is the Shopify product
  price minus the real discount code — keep them in step, or delete the seed
  row and let the Shopify price speak.

  Params:
    product   product object (its handle/title identify the model)
    title     fallback identifier when there is no product
    key       `effective` (price before the coupon) or
              `deal` (price after the coupon, including GST)

  Model matching is the spec seed's: upper-cased, stripped of
  non-alphanumerics, tested as a PREFIX — so `ZEAL Matte Black` is ZEAL.

  Echoes whole rupees, or nothing.
  ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign ident = product.handle | default: title | default: ''
  assign ident = ident | upcase | replace: '-', '' | replace: ' ', '' | replace: '+', '' | replace: '_', ''
  assign alt = product.title | default: title | default: ''
  assign alt = alt | upcase | replace: '-', '' | replace: ' ', '' | replace: '+', '' | replace: '_', ''

  assign model = ''
  assign keys = 'SENTRY,NEXUS,ONYX,ZION,ZEAL' | split: ','
  for k in keys
    assign klen = k | size
    assign head_a = ident | slice: 0, klen
    assign head_b = alt | slice: 0, klen
    if head_a == k or head_b == k
      assign model = k
      break
    endif
  endfor
-%}

{%- if model != blank and key != blank -%}
  {%- capture sheet -%}
    {%- case model -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Only models whose offer pricing the client has actually published
        appear here. A model with no row simply gets nothing — the panel then
        falls back to the Shopify price, or hides. Nothing is invented.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- when 'ZEAL' -%}
effective = 7699
deal = 6200
    {%- endcase -%}
  {%- endcapture -%}
  {%- comment -%} Same `key = value` parser the spec seed uses — one implementation. {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- render 'otodor-spec-seed', seed: sheet, id: key -%}
{%- endif -%}
